<type>(<scope>): <short description>

# Body — explain what changed, why it changed (when useful), important
# implementation details, and any relevant breaking changes.
#
# Supported types:
#   feat      A new feature or capability
#   fix       A bug fix
#   refactor  Code restructuring without behavior change
#   perf      Performance improvement
#   test      Adding or updating tests
#   docs      Documentation-only changes
#   build     Build system or dependency changes
#   ci        CI/CD pipeline or automation changes
#   chore     Maintenance, tooling, or housekeeping
#   revert    Reverting a prior commit
#
# Subject rules:
#   - Concise, imperative mood, no trailing period (e.g. "add", not "added").
#   - Do NOT put agent or model attribution in the subject line.
#
# Breaking changes (if any):
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description of breaking change and migration notes>
#
# Required attribution trailers (for every agent-generated commit):
Agent: <agent name>
Model: <exact model name>
#
# Optional trailers (uncomment only when applicable):
# Supporting-Agents: <agent names>
# Issue: #<number>
#
# Attribution rules:
#   - Never guess the model; use `Unknown` if the runtime does not expose it.
#   - Do not fabricate issue numbers.
#   - Do not add a fake `Co-Authored-By` identity.
#
# Optional local Git setup: git config commit.template .gitmessage
